{
  "requirement": "The harness instructs the model to finish by calling\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.mcp`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation: the harness instructs the model to finish by calling `submit_result` (the form is defined by the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.mcp`, which is context and is not reassessed here). Three marked tests assert the instruction text on the requests actually sent to the model.\n\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` serializes `requests[0].chat_history` and asserts it contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\". This is the generic `ToolAgent` path.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` asserts that all four captured OpenAI-style requests contain \"Finish by calling submit_result\" in `input`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat]` asserts that the `messages` of every captured native Ollama request contain the same text.\n\nAll three assertions check the real request contents. They cover the harness core and both configured backends. The only distinct mode the text governs is the instruction appearing in the prompt, and these tests cover it.\n\nThe tests also check that `submit_result` is offered as a tool and that its schema requires `result`. That falls under `submission.mcp` and goes beyond this subject. The tests carry `{test}` markers for the subject, so there is no marking gap.",
  "references": "6d3090f0bb60675c1ce9da3313f3f3f65297e0a05452744687240cd1bb853491",
